---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContactBand from "../components/ContactBand.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import portrait from "../assets/photos/DSC08683-Edit.jpg";
import { pages } from "../config/compatibility.mjs";
import "../styles/home.css";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Power BI and AI training with Alan | burningsuit"
  description="Power BI and AI training with Alan Harman-Box, for people whose job isn't Power BI. Find a course, or get help with your own reports."
  placeholder={false}
>
  {pages[""].map((id) => <span id={id} aria-hidden="true" />)}
  <div class="home-opening wrap">
    <section class="introduction" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Power BI and AI training · Alan Harman-Box</p>
      <h1 id="page-title">Power BI training for people whose job <span class="em">isn't</span> Power BI.</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">Learn to build a report.<br />Understand what makes it work.</p>
      <p>I teach small groups to build reports, share them and keep them working, and to hand changes to an AI agent (a tool that can read files, make changes and show you what it did) and check what comes back. I explain why things work, so your team can carry on without me.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="#how-i-train">How I train <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="courses" id="training" aria-labelledby="training-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="training-title">Find your starting point</h2>
        <p class="eyebrow">Up to 8 people · teaching files provided</p>
      </div>
      <article class="course" aria-labelledby="fundamentals-title">
        <span class="course-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div>
          <p class="course-fit">New to Power BI?</p>
          <h3 id="fundamentals-title">Power BI fundamentals</h3>
          <p>Build an interactive report, prepare its data so it refreshes, and share it with the people who need it. Day one goes from an Excel table to a shared report; day two is what sits underneath.</p>
          <dl class="course-facts">
            <div><dt>Length</dt><dd>2 days</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Delivery</dt><dd>Private, for your team<br />On site or online · up to 8 people</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="prereq">No Power BI experience, DAX or code needed.</p>
          <div class="course-actions">
            <a class="text-link" href="/training/power-bi-fundamentals/">Read the fundamentals outline</a>
            <a class="text-link" href="/contact/?about=power-bi-fundamentals">Ask about dates</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="course" aria-labelledby="agentic-title">
        <span class="course-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div>
          <p class="course-fit">Already built a report? Start working with an AI agent.</p>
          <h3 id="agentic-title">Agentic development for Power BI 101</h3>
          <p>"Agentic development" just means building with an agent. In one morning you get it to explain a report, write descriptions for its measures (the saved calculations behind the numbers), then build one new measure and check the result.</p>
          <dl class="course-facts">
            <div><dt>Length</dt><dd>Half a day</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Public course</dt><dd><time datetime="2027-01-20">Wednesday 20 January 2027</time> · live online<br />9:30am to 12:30pm UK time · 4 to 8 people</dd></div>
            <div><dt>For a team</dt><dd>Also available as a private course</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="prereq">You've built a report in Power BI Desktop, even a simple one. No code, advanced DAX or agent experience needed.</p>
          <div class="course-actions">
            <a class="text-link" href="/training/agentic-development-for-power-bi/">Read the 101 outline</a>
            <a class="text-link" href="/contact/?about=101">Ask about a seat</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <div class="course-footnote">
        <p>Course prices on request.</p>
        <p>Already building reports and want a day on calculations or table design? DAX fundamentals (1 day) and Data modelling (1 day) and DAX deep dive (2 days) run privately for teams. <a href="/training/">Compare all courses</a></p>
        <p>Not sure which? <a href="/contact/?about=not-sure">Tell me what your team does with Power BI now</a> and I'll suggest where to start.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <figure class="alan-photo">
      <Image src={portrait} alt="Alan Harman-Box smiling, outdoors under trees" widths={[400, 640, 960, 1600]} sizes="(max-width: 680px) calc(100vw - 44px), (max-width: 900px) 40vw, 460px" format="webp" loading="lazy" />
    </figure>
  </div>

  <section id="consultancy" class="consultancy" aria-labelledby="consultancy-title">
    <div class="wrap consultancy-inner">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Consultancy</p><h2 id="consultancy-title">Need help with<br />your own reports?</h2></div>
      <div class="consultancy-copy">
        <p>Courses use prepared teaching files. When the problem is in your own Power BI reports and models, I work alongside your team on them, so the team can look after what we build.</p>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://cal.com/alan-burningsuit/hour">Book a free hour on a call</a>
          <a href="/power-bi/">How consultancy works</a>
          <a href="/work/">See the work</a>
        </div>
        <figure class="proof">
          <figcaption class="eyebrow">The first question I asked a museum's team</figcaption>
          <blockquote><p>"What three metrics, if you could see no others, would actually make a significant difference to what you're doing every day?"</p></blockquote>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how-i-train" class="teaching wrap" aria-labelledby="teaching-title">
    <div class="teaching-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">How I train</p>
      <h2 id="teaching-title">A chance to try.<br />Time to ask.</h2>
      <p>I explain and demonstrate, then you practise on prepared teaching data, with time for questions.</p>
      <p>On the first morning of fundamentals you build a report from an Excel table before anything else, so every later part has a purpose you've already seen. In the 101, you ask an agent to change a report and check what comes back.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/training/how-i-train/">More on how I train</a>
    </div>
    <figure class="exercise">
      <figcaption class="eyebrow">From the 101 course outline</figcaption>
      <h3>One measure.<br />Three checks.</h3>
      <blockquote><p>"Brief one new measure, check its total, a filtered result and an awkward case, give the agent the evidence to correct a wrong answer, and go back to a clean copy when you need to."</p></blockquote>
      <a href="#agentic-title">Back to the 101 <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span></a>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="alan" class="about wrap" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Alan</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="about-title">The person you'll work with</h2>
      <p>I'm Alan Harman-Box, and burningsuit is my solo practice. I've spent about five years working with organisations adopting Power BI and Fabric, after about a decade in software delivery.</p>
      <p>My parents, Stuart and Alison, built burningsuit as a Power BI training business. My mother said it was for "everyone else". They've retired, and I've taken it on.</p>
      <div class="links">
        <a href="/about/">More about me</a>
        <a href="/writing/we-are-all-middle-management-now/">Read: we're all middle management now</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactBand>
    <Fragment slot="heading">Tell me what<br />you're looking for.</Fragment>
    If you know the course, tell me its name and whether you're asking for yourself or a team. If you're unsure where to start, tell me what you need to do with Power BI.
  </ContactBand>
</BaseLayout>
